1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,600
Córdoba, Argentina. October 2020.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,800
NASA satellites spot fires like this from space.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:10,700
Fire Watch turns 26 years of those sightings
into a fire calendar for any place.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,000
Fire moves around the world with the seasons.

5
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:18,400
Fire seasons come at different times
in different places.

6
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,600
The catch: newer satellites pick up far more fire
than the older ones.

7
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:29,500
Fire Watch converts the old counts to the new scale,
so every year can be compared.

8
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:36,000
Now an unusual month stands out.
October 2020 had 2.4× the usual fire activity.

9
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,900
Open that month’s biggest fire day in 3D.

10
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,400
The land and the fire locations are real.
Flames and smoke are simulated.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,800
Tested on years it had never seen, the error
in monthly fire counts drops from 75% to 16%.

12
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:56,300
Pick any place or draw your own area,
in English or Spanish.

13
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:59,900
Fire Watch.
A fire calendar for any place on Earth.
